// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`the bridge keeps its id with the new door (S50b) > cloudEraseHeld is an optional door with no arguments 1`] = `"S50b (US-25 AC16i): a Promise of one word, asked before Disconnect or a switch closes anything. It flushes the open session first, as a close does, then says whether an erase made on this phone is still unsent: 'none' (no session, no such erase, or a save has carried it), 'transient' (its last save failed in a way known to pass: a network call with no answer, a timeout, an abort, 408, 429, a 5xx, or Google's rate or daily limit), 'definite' (the provider refused it: storage full, a refused sign-in, another 4xx) 'unknown' (anything else, a failure no report explained included) or 'expired' (a transient failure 24 hours or more after the erase's first failed send, owner 2026-11-14). Only 'transient' holds the Disconnect; the app runs today's path on every other word and on one it does not know. cloudClose's answers are unchanged. An engine before it has no such door: optionalCall answers nil and Disconnect runs as before, never a crash."`;
